Measure Learning Alongside Closure
A dashboard should help managers decide what needs attention.

Useful measures include:

Time from reporting to initial review.

High-priority actions that are overdue.

Actions awaiting effectiveness verification.

Repeated findings after previous closure.

Reports requiring additional information.

Lessons reviewed by other relevant sites.

Avoid judging performance by report counts alone. An increase in near-miss reporting may reflect greater willingness to speak up. Compare reporting participation, work activity and the nature of the events before drawing conclusions.

