Frequently Asked Questions
Can AI prevent workplace incidents?
AI can support prevention by helping teams identify patterns and prioritise further review. Outcomes depend on data quality, competent decisions and effective controls. AI cannot guarantee that an incident will not occur.

What information should a near-miss report contain?
Include the location, date and time, task underway, event description, potential consequences and immediate action. Add supporting evidence where safe and appropriate.

Does every near miss require the same investigation?
Every report deserves review. The depth of investigation should reflect its potential consequences, recurrence and circumstances, alongside applicable organisational and local requirements.

What is the difference between closing an action and verifying it?
Closing an action records that the assigned work is complete. Verification checks whether the change addresses the identified problem and remains effective in practice.

